    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for that. i guess i'm wondering though... when people argue against it, it usually just feels like they're being resistant to basic respect or trying to cling to outdated ideas. do you think the \"confusion\" argument is actually a valid concern for a modern business, or is it just a way for people to avoid being inclusive?",
